    "result_text": "Full build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for `POST /api/owners`: when more than 80 owners have already been created for the new owner's registration day, the response (and subsequent `GET`) includes `bulkSignupWarning: true`, otherwise `false`.\n\nBecause owners are read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, the flag is computed at creation and **persisted on the entity** (same pattern as `namesakeCount`, `customerCode`), not recomputed at read time.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the readOnly `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 new `bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`AssignBulkSignupWarning.java`** (new OfficeFloor function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's effective (business-day-adjusted) date and sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. Runs before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner isn't counted against itself, mirroring the daily-limit accumulation path.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignBulkWarning` step (under `transaction` governance) between `assignNamesake` and `save`.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`/`h2`/`mysql`/`postgres`) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column; fixed the hsqldb positional seed INSERTs (the test DB) by appending the new column value.\n\nMapStruct auto-wires the field by name (no mapper change needed). `AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` and the full suite pass.",
